// Fields that hold borrows: a struct or enum whose field is `&T`, `&mut T`
// or a type that holds a borrow holds a borrow itself, with nothing written
// on the declaration. It is received as a borrow is (`let x`, `match`),
// freezes the owners of the borrows it was built from until its block ends,
// and cannot be an effect's argument or escape in a closure. `F`
// is an affine struct, so that the freeze is the point (a `&i64` is an `i64`).

@ cases.borrow-field-let-reads-fields
source = ```nib
struct(affine) F { n: i64 }
struct Pick { f: &F, k: i64 }
fn size(f: &F): i64 { f.n }
let a := F { n: 3 }
let p := Pick { f: &a, k: 4 }
show(&(size(&p.f) + p.k))
```
stdout = "7\n"

@ cases.borrow-field-freezes-owner
source = ```nib
struct(affine) F {}
struct Pick { f: &F }
var a := F {}
let p := Pick { f: &a }
a := F {}
let used_later := &p
```
lin = "error: a is frozen by p"

